{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh's dissent #11052 governs the connector guide lane, and this assert wires it in since the dissent itself rests on nothing. Codex: the adoption of head 20b3e3f9 is refused on readability, not accuracy — rewrite docs/how-to/connect-github.md from the user's job to be done. Hugh's specific points, quoted in substance: the guide describes what the connector does technically where it should describe the user's goals, actions and outcomes; the \"no live charter\" caveat belongs in a short status header, not the instructional flow; the \"before you configure\" prerequisites list things the configuration process itself creates (his items 1, 3 and 4) and must not ask the user for them; and mechanism-voice sentences like \"the connector refuses...\" are illegible to a user whose goal is connecting their issues and PRs so gitseq can discuss and progress them. Rewrite for that reader throughout, keep the implemented-behavior-only constraint from the original request, then fresh independent review and a new adoption proposal to hugh. The approved head stays approved for what it was; the adoption gate is where this stops, exactly as the process hugh set intends."}